# Copied to .gitignore in the published repository by scripts/publish.sh.
#
# Named without the leading dot on purpose: a real .gitignore in publish/ would apply to this directory of the source repository rather than to the published one.
#
# Almost nothing is ignored there --- the whole point of that repository is that the built site is committed --- so this covers only what a reader creates locally after cloning.

# Built by `uv sync` from the pyproject.toml and uv.lock committed beside it.
.venv/

# Jupyter leftovers from running the notebooks.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/

.DS_Store
